0.078 g
56.6929133858267775 606.8978740157480161 Td
(Answer:) Tj
T* (The First Law of Thermodynamics states that energy can neither be created nor destroyed; heat supplied to a closed system equals the) Tj
T* (sum of the increase in its internal energy and the work done by the system on its surroundings.) Tj
T* (Mathematical formulation: dQ = dU + dW = dU + P dV) Tj
T* (Where: dQ = infinitesimal heat absorbed by the system \(Joules\), dU = infinitesimal change in internal energy \(Joules\), and dW = P dV =) Tj
T* (mechanical work done by the system against external pressure P \(Joules\).) Tj
