(Q: Derive an analytical expression for the work done during the reversible isothermal expansion of n moles of an) Tj
T* (ideal gas from volume V1 to volume V2 at temperature T.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.078 g
56.6929133858267775 440.5041732283464171 Td
(Answer:) Tj
T* (1. Condition: In an isothermal process, temperature T remains constant \(Delta T = 0\), so Delta U = 0 for an ideal gas.) Tj
T* (2. Work done for differential volume change dV: dW = P dV.) Tj
T* (3. Using the ideal gas equation of state: P = n R T / V.) Tj
T* (4. Integrating from initial volume V1 to final volume V2:) Tj
T* (   W = Integral [V1 to V2] P dV = Integral [V1 to V2] \(n R T / V\) dV = n R T Integral [V1 to V2] \(1 / V\) dV) Tj
T* (5. Evaluating the integral: W = n R T [ln\(V\)]_[V1 to V2] = n R T ln\(V2 / V1\).) Tj
T* (6. Converting to base-10 logarithm:) Tj
T* (   W = 2.303 n R T log10\(V2 / V1\).) Tj
T* (␀7␀.␀ ␀I␀n␀ ␀t␀e␀r␀m␀s␀ ␀o␀f␀ ␀p␀r␀e␀s␀s␀u␀r␀e␀s␀ ␀\(␀u␀s␀i␀n␀g␀ ␀B␀o␀y␀l␀e␀’␀s␀ ␀l␀a␀w␀ ␀P␀1␀ ␀V␀1␀ ␀=␀ ␀P␀2␀ ␀V␀2␀ !Ò␀ ␀V␀2␀ ␀/␀ ␀V␀1␀ ␀=␀ ␀P␀1␀ ␀/␀ ␀P␀2␀\)␀:) Tj
T* (   W = 2.303 n R T log10\(P1 / P2\).) Tj
