(Q: Describe the working of a Carnot engine. Explain the four reversible stages of the Carnot cycle with the aid of a) Tj
T* (neat P-V indicator diagram, and derive the expression for its thermal efficiency eta = 1 - \(Tc / Th\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.078 g
56.6929133858267775 207.4962992125983874 Td
(Answer:) Tj
T* (A Carnot engine is an idealized, reversible heat engine operating between a heat source at Th and a heat sink at Tc.) Tj
T* (The four successive stages on the P-V diagram are:) Tj
T* (1. Stage 1 \(A -> B\): Reversible Isothermal Expansion at constant source temperature Th. Gas absorbs heat Qh from the source and) Tj
T* (expands from VA to VB. Work done: W1 = Qh = n R Th ln\(VB / VA\).) Tj
T* (2. Stage 2 \(B -> C\): Reversible Adiabatic Expansion from Th to Tc. Gas expands without heat exchange from VB to VC, doing work W2) Tj
T* (= n R \(Th - Tc\) / \(gamma - 1\). Adiabatic relation: Th VB^\(gamma-1\) = Tc VC^\(gamma-1\) ... \(Eq. 1\).) Tj
T* (3. Stage 3 \(C -> D\): Reversible Isothermal Compression at constant sink temperature Tc. Gas is compressed from VC to VD, rejecting) Tj
T* (heat Qc to the sink. Work done: W3 = -Qc = -n R Tc ln\(VC / VD\).) Tj
T* (4. Stage 4 \(D -> A\): Reversible Adiabatic Compression from Tc to Th. Gas is compressed without heat exchange from VD to VA,) Tj
T* (restoring initial state A. Work done: W4 = -n R \(Th - Tc\) / \(gamma - 1\). Adiabatic relation: Tc VD^\(gamma-1\) = Th VA^\(gamma-1\) ... \(Eq.) Tj
T* (2\).) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Net Work & Efficiency Derivation:) Tj
T* (Net work: W_net = W1 + W2 + W3 + W4. Since W2 + W4 = 0, W_net = W1 + W3 = Qh - Qc.) Tj
T* (␀D␀i␀v␀i␀d␀i␀n␀g␀ ␀E␀q␀.␀ ␀1␀ ␀b␀y␀ ␀E␀q␀.␀ ␀2␀:␀ ␀\(␀V␀B␀ ␀/␀ ␀V␀A␀\)␀^␀\(␀g␀a␀m␀m␀a␀-␀1␀\)␀ ␀=␀ ␀\(␀V␀C␀ ␀/␀ ␀V␀D␀\)␀^␀\(␀g␀a␀m␀m␀a␀-␀1␀\)␀ !Ò␀ ␀V␀B␀ ␀/␀ ␀V␀A␀ ␀=␀ ␀V␀C␀ ␀/␀ ␀V␀D␀.) Tj
T* (Therefore, the heat ratio simplifies to: Qc / Qh = [n R Tc ln\(VC / VD\)] / [n R Th ln\(VB / VA\)] = Tc / Th.) Tj
T* (Thermal efficiency is defined as: eta = W_net / Qh = \(Qh - Qc\) / Qh = 1 - \(Qc / Qh\).) Tj
T* (Substituting Qc / Qh = Tc / Th:) Tj
T* (eta_carnot = 1 - \(Tc / Th\).) Tj
